  "title": "Strong colorability",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $r$ be a positive integer. We say that a graph $G$ is strongly $r$-colorable if for every partition of the vertices to sets of size at most $r$ there is a proper $r$-coloring of $G$ in which the vertices in each set of the partition have distinct colors.\n\nConjecture If $\\Delta$ is the maximal degree of a graph $G$, then $G$ is strongly $2 \\Delta$-colorable.",
